    <!-- About -->
    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_statement">NAYON Browser is developed by MD. AHOSHAN HABIB NAYON. It is a privacy-respecting Android browser built with Kotlin and Jetpack Compose.</string>

    <!-- Privacy -->
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_draft_notice">Draft — this describes the current Stage 2 build and will be updated as features are added. It is not yet a final legal policy.</string>
    <string name="privacy_section_summary">Summary</string>
    <string name="privacy_summary">NAYON Browser is developed by MD. AHOSHAN HABIB NAYON. Website: https://webtecit.com. NAYON Browser may process browsing data locally to provide browser functionality. If optional cloud synchronization, authentication, search suggestions, payment integrations or other connected services are enabled, relevant data may be processed by the selected providers according to their policies. Sensitive credentials must be protected by the implemented security architecture. Private browsing does not make you completely anonymous online. Review the Privacy Policy and individual permission settings before using optional services.</string>
    <string name="privacy_section_current">What this build stores</string>
    <string name="privacy_current">Stored only on this device: your settings, browsing history and bookmarks (normal tabs only), open normal tabs if “Restore tabs” is on, and cookies, site data and cache created by websites you visit. None of it is included in Android cloud backup or device transfer.</string>
    <string name="privacy_section_not_collected">What this build does not do</string>
    <string name="privacy_not_collected">NAYON Browser contains no analytics, advertising or tracking SDKs and sends nothing to the developer. Websites you open receive your requests directly. Your search words go to the search engine you choose; with Search suggestions on, typed text is also sent to it (never in private tabs). Home-page shortcut icons are downloaded once from each shortcut\'s own website. When Google Safe Browsing is available on your device, Android System WebView may check site addresses with Google to warn you about dangerous sites. Private tabs are not saved to history.</string>
    <string name="privacy_section_deletion">Deleting your data</string>
    <string name="privacy_deletion">Use Settings → Clear browsing data, delete single items in History and Bookmarks, or clear the app\'s storage in Android settings. Uninstalling removes everything.</string>
    <string name="privacy_section_changes">Changes</string>
    <string name="privacy_changes">When browsing, history, downloads, passwords or optional connected services are added, this policy will be updated to describe exactly what is collected, where it is stored, how long it is kept and how to delete it.</string>

